<%# The signed-in right side of the navbar. This SHADOWS studio-engine's
    components/_user_nav (a host view wins in this non-isolated engine), for
    three things that partial has no setting for (task cyvasse-contrast-and-names):

    - One theme toggle on a phone. The engine's navbar already draws one in
      its phone row, so this one is desktop only, as the engine's own
      signed-out bar does it.
    - One tab stop. The name and the avatar are one link to the profile, not
      two links to the same page.
    - On a phone, the avatar alone, so the name never truncates to "Guest 55…".
      The name stays in the link as screen-reader text.

    The name is the player's one public name (User#player_name).

    Cyvasse players have no balance, wallet or level, so the engine partial's
    second row never rendered here; its slot locals are accepted and unused.
    Delete this file once the engine partial does the above. %>
<% name = current_user.player_name %>
<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
  <%= render "components/admin_dropdown" unless respond_to?(:studio_sidebar_replaces_admin_menu?) && studio_sidebar_replaces_admin_menu? %>
  <span class="hidden md:flex" data-nav-theme-toggle="desktop"><%= render "components/theme_toggle_morph" %></span>
  <%= link_to profile_path, class: "group flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0 hover:opacity-80 transition", data: { nav_account: true } do %>
    <span class="sr-only md:not-sr-only md:min-w-0"><span class="block truncate text-heading font-semibold text-base leading-none" data-nav-name><%= name %></span></span>
    <span class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center" aria-hidden="true">
      <%= render "components/avatar", user: current_user, size: "nav" %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
</div>
